      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We measured growth hormone-related substances in patients with angina pectoris precipitated by different underlying disorders. Although hyperinsulinemia was more pronounced in patients with angina pectoris secondary to atherosclerotic coronary disease than in patients with syndrome X and variant angina, we found no evidence that growth hormone-related substances including insulin-like growth factor-I are associated with coronary atherosclerosis."},
